ents, circuit boards, and scrap materials. Use your scrapping hammer to break down equipment and build the tools needed to repair the station's communications array and call for rescue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3847850/extras/d67a07e6acc1879955eed8c609afda42.poster.avif?t=1755629088\" width=616 height=216 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3847850/extras/d67a07e6acc1879955eed8c609afda42.webm?t=1755629088\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3847850/extras/d67a07e6acc1879955eed8c609afda42.mp4?t=1755629088\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>BATTLE THE ELEMENTS</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Antarctica doesn't forgive. Monitor your body temperature as the brutal cold saps your strength. Find portable stoves, warm clothing, and shelter to stave off hypothermia that will slow your movement and leave you vulnerable.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>KEY FEATURES:</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No-combat survival horror</strong> inspired by Alien: Isolation and Amnesia: The Bunker</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Advanced AI predator</strong> that tracks your light sources and investigates sounds</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Environmental storytelling</strong> revealing the dark secrets of Erebus Station</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Realistic cold survival mechanics</strong> with hypothermia effects</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Scrapping and crafting system</strong> to repair critical equipment</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiple detection tools</strong> including H2S detectors and binoculars to track the creature</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic hiding system</strong> with interactive cover points throughout the station</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric Antarctic setting</strong> with realistic weather and isolation</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A MYSTERY FROZEN IN TIME</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Uncover the truth behind the creature's awakening and the fate of the research team. As you piece together the station's final days through environmental clues and scattered notes, you'll discover that some secrets are better left buried in the ice.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Conrad, the station's mechanic and lone survivor, offers refuge in his barricaded cabin\u2014but in a place where trust is as scarce as warmth, even allies may harbor deadly intentions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can you repair the communications, survive the creature's hunt, and escape the frozen hell of Erebus Station?</strong></p>",
